## Poetry Setup: Dependency Management: Yeh project ke saare Python packages aur libraries (jaise 
psycopg2, gunicorn, etc.) ko ek hi jagah manage karta hai aur pyproject.toml
file ki madad se exact versions ko track karta hai.
Isolated Environment:


# Remove old Ubuntu Poetry package if present:
sudo apt remove -y python3-poetry

# Install current Poetry version:
curl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python3 -

# Add Poetry to your PATH and reload configuration:
echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

# Verify Poetry and configure Python 3.11:
poetry --version
poetry env use /usr/bin/python3.11
poetry env info

# Install Dependencies and Gunicorn:
poetry install --no-root

# Verify psycopg2 can be imported successfully:
poetry run python -c "import psycopg2; print('psycopg2 OK')"

# Add and verify Gunicorn:
poetry add Gunicorn
poetry run gunicorn --version

